# Desktop UI

Keep the PySide6 shell. Do not rewrite it.

- Heavy work uses `Worker` from `src/claynext/core/worker.py` on `QThreadPool`. Change widgets only through signals.
- Colors and type come from `src/claynext/constants/theme_constants.py`. No ad-hoc QSS colors.
- Chrome: `CUSTOM_WINDOW_CHROME` in `src/claynext/constants/ui_constants.py`. Windows is frameless; macOS and Linux stay native unless `CLAYNEXT_CUSTOM_CHROME=1`.
- Widget skill: `.agents/skills/claynext-ui-component/SKILL.md`.
- A dataset review queue (JOB-006) is read-only first and uses the worker pattern.
